{"text": "Plainspoken HR Consulting - INVESTIGATION WORKING NOTES - PRIVILEGED AT DIRECTION OF COUNSEL\nClient: Cobblestone Brewing Supply Co., Asheville warehouse      Matter no. PHR-25-031\nInvestigator: Loretta Hsieh, SPHR       Notes typed same day from handwritten; quotes are as close as I could get them.\n\nCOMPLAINT RECEIVED 10/27/25 via the ethics line (ticket EL-00418). Complainant Imani Braxton-Reid, inventory lead, emp. ID 20771, hired March 2021.\nRespondent Douglas Krantz (\"Dougie\"), second-shift warehouse supervisor, emp. ID 10388, with the company 14 yrs.\nPolicy at issue: Policy 4.2 (harassment), Title VII categories religion / sex / sexual orientation.\n\n--- INTERVIEW 1: I. Braxton-Reid, Mon. Nov 3, 9:05-10:20, conf. room B. Gave Upjohn-style notice; she declined to have anyone with her.\n\n- Imani says it started in August after she began wearing a hijab to work. She converted to Islam last spring. Before that, she says, Krantz \"was fine with me.\"\n- First incident she can date: Aug. 19, shift huddle. Krantz allegedly said \"is that thing OSHA approved?\" and tugged at the back of the scarf. Others laughed. She told him not to touch her.\n- 9/11: he said over the radio, \"somebody keep an eye on Imani today.\" She says at least six people were on channel 2.\n- Since then he calls her \"Sister Mary\" in front of the crew. She has asked him to stop twice.\n- 10/24 (the Friday before she called the line): she asked for the small office for five minutes to pray. He said, \"You can pray on your own time, this isn't a mosque,\" and wrote her up for an unauthorized break the same afternoon. I have the write-up (form dated 10/24, signed D. Krantz).\n- She also raised, without my asking, how he treats Feliciano Manalastas on the dock. She says Krantz calls him \"princess\" and once said he \"didn't want Chano in the locker room with the guys.\" She says Chano is gay and not out to most people at work, and she is worried she has now outed him to me. I told her I would handle that carefully.\n- Effect on her: not sleeping; her doctor put her on sertraline in October; she has used four sick days. She is looking at other jobs.\n- Wants: for it to stop, the write-up removed, and not to be moved off second shift (she shares custody and the schedule is built around it).\n- Personal cell for follow-up, NOT work email: 828-555-0173, imani.breid@blueridgemail.example.\n\n--- INTERVIEW 2: Bree Tolbert, picker, 11/3, 10:40-11:05\n\n- Was at the Aug. 19 huddle. Confirms the \"OSHA approved\" remark and that he \"kind of flicked\" the scarf. \"Everybody laughed because it's Dougie, that's how he is.\"\n- Has heard \"Sister Mary\" \"a bunch.\" Did not hear the radio comment.\n- Asked whether she has seen him treat others differently: long pause. \"He rides Chano pretty hard. I don't want to say why.\"\n- Bree is nervous. She is Krantz's niece by marriage and asked me three times who would see these notes.\n\n--- INTERVIEW 3: F. Manalastas, Tues. 11/4, 14:00-14:35, by phone at his request (828.555.0109)\n\n- Did not want to be interviewed. Says he \"has no complaint.\" Confirms \"princess.\" Says it \"doesn't bother him.\"\n- On the locker room remark: \"Who told you that?\" then, after a while, \"Yeah. He said it. In July.\"\n- Volunteered that he is here on a green card through his husband and \"cannot afford trouble.\" I told him retaliation is prohibited and gave him my direct line.\n- He overheard the radio comment on 9/11 and says Zoran Milićević (maintenance) said on the channel, \"Not cool, Doug.\"\n\n--- INTERVIEW 4: Douglas Krantz, Wed. Nov. 5, 15:30-16:50. Ansel Corrigan (HR manager) sat in.\n\n- Denies touching the scarf. \"I pointed at it.\" Says the OSHA comment was a real question about loose clothing near the conveyor.\n- \"Sister Mary\": admits it. \"It's a joke. She used to laugh.\" Could not say when she last laughed.\n- Radio comment: \"I say that about everybody.\" Could not name another person he has said it about.\n- The 10/24 write-up: says she had already had both breaks. Time-clock report shows one break that day, not two. He had no answer.\n- \"Princess\": \"That's just dock talk.\" Locker room remark: denies it flatly.\n- Raised his own issues: says he has been under strain, his wife is in chemo, and he is \"six years sober and not about to lose this job over a nickname.\"\n- File check with Mr. Corrigan afterwards: Krantz has a written warning from 2022 for a comment about a Hispanic temp's accent. He did not mention it when I asked about prior discipline.\n\nPRELIMINARY VIEW (for counsel only): the complainant is credible and largely corroborated. Recommend removing the 10/24 write-up now, separating reporting lines pending findings, and no contact between Krantz and either witness. Draft report to Ansel by November 14. Fee to date $4,275 (22.5 hrs at $190).\nLH", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "825 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Loretta Hsieh", "Imani Braxton-Reid", "Douglas Krantz", "Imani", "Krantz", "Feliciano Manalastas", "Bree Tolbert", "Dougie", "Sister Mary", "Bree", "F. Manalastas", "Zoran Milićević", "Mr. Corrigan"], "companies": ["Plainspoken HR Consulting", "Cobblestone Brewing Supply Co.", " OSHA", "Blue Ridge", "OSHA", "Krantz"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Asheville", "warehouse", "Aug.", "July", "9/11"], "health": ["not sleeping", "sertraline", "sick days", "chemo", "six years sober"], "sensitive": ["religion", "sex", "sexual orientation", "Islam", "hijab", "pray", "gay", "heterosexual", "green card", "cannot afford trouble", "Hispanic", "nickname", "accent"], "names": ["Imani", "Douglas", "Dougie", "Krantz", "Feliciano", "Bree", "Tolbert", "Doug", "F.", "Zoran", "Mary", "Princess"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 4, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn",